# README Alignment Rules (WatchAgent)

- README must stay aligned with the assignment-required sections: system
  overview, architecture visualization, setup/run instructions, API reference,
  test instructions, technology choices, event detection design, and Cursor
  Setup.
- If an event type is added, removed, renamed, or has a trigger changed, update
  the README Event Detection Design section and the event tests in the same
  change.
- If Docker commands, environment variables, ports, or database paths change,
  update setup/run instructions immediately.
- If Cursor rules, agents, or skills change, update the Cursor Setup section so
  a reviewer can understand why each artifact exists and how to run skills.
- Avoid adding extra assignment-review documents or generated artifacts unless
  the user explicitly asks for them. Keep the final submission focused on the
  required repository files.
- README examples should be honest: do not imply live events are guaranteed
  during a short runtime window, because the event logic is transition-based.
